//!
//! # Boot
//!
//! What the bootloader hands to the kernel: the Limine requests and responses
//! and the higher half direct map.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name           | File          | Purpose                                                   |
//! |----------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Boot::Limine` | `limine.ign`  | the requests the kernel makes, the response layouts, typed readers |
//! | `Boot::Hhdm`   | `hhdm.ign`    | physical address to direct-map pointer                    |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! None in the kernel. `Boot` only reads memory that Limine wrote, so every
//! subsystem that needs boot information may import it:
//!
//! ```ignis
//! import Boot from "@boot";
//!
//! let memmap: *mut Boot::Limine::MemmapResponse = Boot::Limine::memmap();
//! ```
//!
//! The Limine modules are not here. Mapping them needs the virtual memory
//! manager, so `Mm::Modules` owns them.

import _ from "./hhdm";
import _ from "./limine";

/// Aggregate namespace of the boot information. The files above contribute
/// `Boot::Limine` and `Boot::Hhdm`.
export namespace Boot {}
